(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Change the order of integration and evaluate the non-elementary integral: I = int_0^1 int_y^1 e^\(x^2\) dx dy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Analyze the original region of integration:) Tj
T*
(   - Inner limits: x varies from x = y to x = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Outer limits: y varies from y = 0 to y = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - The integrand e^\(x^2\) has no elementary antiderivative with respect to x.) Tj
T*
(   - Bounding lines of region R:) Tj
T*
(   Left boundary: line x = y \(or y = x\).) Tj
T*
(   Right boundary: vertical line x = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Bottom boundary: horizontal line y = 0.) Tj
T*
(   The region is a triangle with vertices \(0, 0\), \(1, 0\), and \(1, 1\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Change Order of Integration \(Vertical slicing\):) Tj
T*
(   - Now let x vary over the whole outer interval: x in [0, 1].) Tj
T*
(   - For each fixed x, y varies vertically from the bottom axis y = 0 to the upper line y = x:) Tj
T*
(   0 <= y <= x.) Tj
T*
(   - The transformed integral is:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^1 [ int_0^x e^\(x^2\) dy ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Inner Integral with respect to y:) Tj
T*
(   Since e^\(x^2\) does not depend on y:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^x e^\(x^2\) dy = e^\(x^2\) * [ y ]_0^x = e^\(x^2\) * \(x - 0\) = x * e^\(x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate the Outer Integral with respect to x:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^1 x * e^\(x^2\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute u = x^2 => du = 2x dx => x dx = du / 2.) Tj
T*
(   When x = 0, u = 0; when x = 1, u = 1.) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^1 e^u * \(du / 2\) = \(1/2\) * [ e^u ]_0^1) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * \(e^1 - e^0\) = \(1/2\) * \(e - 1\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   By changing the order of integration, the non-elementary integral is resolved to \(e - 1\) / 2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
