(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the polar coordinate transformation for double integrals. Use polar coordinates to evaluate the famous improper integral: I = int_0^infinity int_0^infinity e^\(-\(x^2 + y^2\)\) dx dy, and hence deduce the value of the Gaussian integral int_0^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Polar Area Element:) Tj
T*
(   - Transformation: x = r * cos theta, y = r * sin theta.) Tj
T*
(   - The Jacobian of transformation J = d\(x, y\) / d\(r, theta\) is:) Tj
T*
