(   J = det\([ dx/dr, dx/dtheta; dy/dr, dy/dtheta ]\) = det\([ cos theta, -r*sin theta; sin theta,) Tj
T*
(   r*cos theta ]\)) Tj
T*
(   = r * cos^2 theta + r * sin^2 theta = r.) Tj
T*
(   - By the change of variables theorem for multiple integrals:) Tj
T*
(   iint_R f\(x, y\) dx dy = iint_{R'} f\(r*cos theta, r*sin theta\) * |J| dr dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = iint_{R'} f\(r*cos theta, r*sin theta\) * r dr dtheta. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Evaluation of Double Integral over First Quadrant:) Tj
T*
(   - Region R: x in [0, infinity\), y in [0, infinity\) \(first quadrant of the plane\).) Tj
T*
(   - In polar coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   Radial coordinate r ranges from 0 to infinity.) Tj
T*
(   Angular coordinate theta ranges from 0 to pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - x^2 + y^2 = r^2.) Tj
T*
(   - I = int_0^\(pi/2\) [ int_0^infinity e^\(-r^2\) * r dr ] dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Inner integral: int_0^infinity e^\(-r^2\) * r dr:) Tj
T*
(   Let u = r^2, du = 2r dr => r dr = du / 2.) Tj
T*
(   int_0^infinity e^\(-u\) * \(du / 2\) = \(1/2\) * [-e^\(-u\)]_0^infinity = \(1/2\) * \(0 - \(-1\)\) = 1/2.) Tj
T*
(   - Outer integral:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^\(pi/2\) \(1/2\) dtheta = \(1/2\) * [ theta ]_0^\(pi/2\) = \(1/2\) * \(pi / 2\) = pi / 4.) Tj
T*
(   3. Deduction of the Gaussian Integral:) Tj
T*
(   - Notice that the double integral factors into two identical independent single integrals:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx * int_0^infinity e^\(-y^2\) dy = [ int_0^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx ]^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Since I = pi / 4:) Tj
T*
(   [ int_0^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx ]^2 = pi / 4.) Tj
T*
(   - Taking the positive square root:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx = sqrt\(pi\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - By symmetry of the even integrand:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-infinity}^infinity e^\(-x^2\) dx = 2 * \(sqrt\(pi\) / 2\) = sqrt\(pi\).) Tj
T*
