(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the double integral: I = iint_R sqrt\(a^2 - x^2 - y^2\) dx dy, where R is the region in the first quadrant enclosed by the circle x^2 + y^2 = a^2, by transforming into polar coordinates.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the Polar Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   - x = r * cos theta, y = r * sin theta.) Tj
T*
(   - Area element: dx dy = r dr dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrand: sqrt\(a^2 - \(x^2 + y^2\)\) = sqrt\(a^2 - r^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Determine Limits of Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - The region R is the first quadrant of the circular disk of radius a.) Tj
T*
(   - r varies from 0 to a.) Tj
T*
(   - theta varies from 0 to pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Formulate the Transformed Integral:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^\(pi/2\) [ int_0^a sqrt\(a^2 - r^2\) * r dr ] dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate the Radial \(Inner\) Integral:) Tj
T*
(   Let K = int_0^a sqrt\(a^2 - r^2\) * r dr.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute u = a^2 - r^2 => du = -2r dr => r dr = -du / 2.) Tj
T*
(   When r = 0, u = a^2; when r = a, u = 0.) Tj
T*
(   K = int_{a^2}^0 u^\(1/2\) * \(-du / 2\) = \(1/2\) * int_0^\(a^2\) u^\(1/2\) du) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * [ u^\(3/2\) / \(3/2\) ]_0^\(a^2\) = \(1/2\) * \(2/3\) * [ \(a^2\)^\(3/2\) - 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/3\) * a^3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Evaluate the Angular \(Outer\) Integral:) Tj
T*
(   I = int_0^\(pi/2\) K dtheta = int_0^\(pi/2\) \(a^3 / 3\) dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = \(a^3 / 3\) * [ theta ]_0^\(pi/2\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(a^3 / 3\) * \(pi / 2\) = pi * a^3 / 6.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
