(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Using double integration, find the area enclosed between the parabola y = x^2 and the straight line y = 2x.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Find Points of Intersection:) Tj
T*
(   Set x^2 = 2x => x^2 - 2x = 0 => x * \(x - 2\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Roots: x = 0 and x = 2.) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 0: y = 0. Point O\(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 2: y = 4. Point P\(2, 4\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Determine Upper and Lower Boundaries on [0, 2]:) Tj
T*
(   For any test point in \(0, 2\), e.g., x = 1:) Tj
T*
(   y_line = 2\(1\) = 2.) Tj
T*
(   y_parabola = 1^2 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Since 2 > 1, the upper curve is y = 2x and the lower curve is y = x^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Set up the Double Integral:) Tj
T*
(   Area A = iint_R 1 dA = int_0^2 [ int_{x^2}^{2x} dy ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate the Inner Integral:) Tj
T*
(   int_{x^2}^{2x} dy = [ y ]_{x^2}^{2x} = 2x - x^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Evaluate the Outer Integral:) Tj
T*
(   A = int_0^2 \(2x - x^2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2*\(x^2 / 2\) - x^3 / 3 ]_0^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ x^2 - x^3 / 3 ]_0^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2^2 - 2^3 / 3 ] - 0) Tj
T*
(   = 4 - 8/3 = 12/3 - 8/3 = 4/3.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The area enclosed between the parabola and the line is 4/3 square units.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Using double integration in polar coordinates, calculate the area of the region bounded by the cardioid r = a * \(1 + cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the Polar Area Integral:) Tj
T*
(   Area A = iint_R dA = iint_R r dr dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Limits of Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - By symmetry about the initial line theta = 0, the total area is twice the area of the upper) Tj
T*
(   half:) Tj
T*
(   A = 2 * int_0^pi [ int_0^{a\(1 + cos theta\)} r dr ] dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Inner \(Radial\) Integral:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^{a\(1 + cos theta\)} r dr = [ r^2 / 2 ]_0^{a\(1 + cos theta\)} = \(a^2 / 2\) * \(1 + cos) Tj
T*
(   theta\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Substitute into Outer Integral:) Tj
T*
(   A = 2 * int_0^pi [ \(a^2 / 2\) * \(1 + cos theta\)^2 ] dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * int_0^pi \(1 + 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Use half-angle formula cos^2 theta = \(1 + cos 2theta\) / 2:) Tj
T*
(   1 + 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta = 1 + 2*cos theta + 1/2 + \(1/2\)*cos 2theta) Tj
T*
(   = 3/2 + 2*cos theta + \(1/2\)*cos 2theta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Integrate from 0 to pi:) Tj
T*
(   A = a^2 * [ \(3/2\)*theta + 2*sin theta + \(1/4\)*sin 2theta ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
ET

