(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive formulas for the center of mass \(centroid\) and moments of inertia of a plane lamina R using double integration. Find the centroid of the region bounded by the parabola y^2 = 4ax and its latus rectum x = a.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. General Formulas for Centroid \(Uniform Density rho = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   - Total Area: A = iint_R dA.) Tj
T*
(   - First moments: M_y = iint_R x dA, M_x = iint_R y dA.) Tj
T*
(   - Centroid coordinates: x_bar = M_y / A, y_bar = M_x / A.) Tj
T*
(   2. Centroid of Region Bounded by y^2 = 4ax and x = a:) Tj
T*
(   - Symmetry: The region is bounded by y = -2*sqrt\(ax\) to y = +2*sqrt\(ax\) from x = 0 to x = a.) Tj
T*
(   Since the region is symmetric about the x-axis \(y = 0\), the centroid must lie on the x-axis:) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute Area A:) Tj
T*
(   A = int_0^a [ int_{-2*sqrt\(ax\)}^{2*sqrt\(ax\)} dy ] dx = int_0^a 4*sqrt\(a\)*x^\(1/2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = 4*sqrt\(a\) * [ x^\(3/2\) / \(3/2\) ]_0^a = \(8/3\)*sqrt\(a\) * a^\(3/2\) = \(8/3\)*a^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute First Moment M_y:) Tj
T*
(   M_y = iint_R x dA = int_0^a x * [ 4*sqrt\(a\)*x^\(1/2\) ] dx = 4*sqrt\(a\) * int_0^a x^\(3/2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = 4*sqrt\(a\) * [ x^\(5/2\) / \(5/2\) ]_0^a = \(8/5\)*sqrt\(a\) * a^\(5/2\) = \(8/5\)*a^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute x_bar:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = M_y / A = [ \(8/5\)*a^3 ] / [ \(8/3\)*a^2 ] = \(8/5\) * \(3/8\) * a = 3a / 5.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The centroid coordinates are \(x_bar, y_bar\) = \(3a / 5, 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the moment of inertia of a uniform circular disc of mass M and radius R about: \(i\) An axis perpendicular to the disc through its center \(polar moment of inertia\), and \(ii\) Any diameter.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Mass and Density of Disc:) Tj
T*
(   - Area of circular disc = pi * R^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Surface density \(mass per unit area\): rho = M / \(pi * R^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Polar Moment of Inertia I_0 \(about perpendicular central axis\):) Tj
T*
(   - I_0 = iint_R r^2 * rho dA.) Tj
T*
(   - In polar coordinates: dA = r dr dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   r ranges from 0 to R; theta ranges from 0 to 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(   - I_0 = rho * int_0^\(2*pi\) [ int_0^R r^3 dr ] dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = rho * [ theta ]_0^\(2*pi\) * [ r^4 / 4 ]_0^R) Tj
T*
(   = rho * \(2*pi\) * \(R^4 / 4\) = \(pi * rho * R^4\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute rho = M / \(pi * R^2\):) Tj
T*
(   I_0 = [ pi * \(M / \(pi * R^2\)\) * R^4 ] / 2 = \(1/2\) * M * R^2. \(Part i proved\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Moment of Inertia about a Diameter:) Tj
T*
(   - By symmetry: I_x = I_y \(moments of inertia about any two perpendicular diameters are equal\).) Tj
T*
(   - By the Perpendicular Axis Theorem for planar laminae:) Tj
T*
(   I_0 = I_x + I_y = 2 * I_x.) Tj
T*
(   - Solve for I_x:) Tj
T*
(   I_x = I_0 / 2 = [ \(1/2\) * M * R^2 ] / 2 = \(1/4\) * M * R^2.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
