(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the volume of the tetrahedron bounded by the coordinate planes x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 and the plane x + y + z = 1 using triple integration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the Triple Integral:) Tj
T*
(   Volume V = iiint_V 1 dx dy dz.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Determine Limits of Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - The plane is z = 1 - x - y.) Tj
T*
(   - The bottom face is the xy-plane \(z = 0\). Thus z varies from 0 to 1 - x - y.) Tj
T*
(   - In the xy-plane \(z = 0\), the boundary is x + y = 1 => y = 1 - x.) Tj
T*
(   Thus y varies from 0 to 1 - x.) Tj
T*
(   - Along the x-axis \(y = 0\), the intercept is x = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Thus x varies from 0 to 1.) Tj
T*
(   V = int_0^1 [ int_0^\(1 - x\) [ int_0^\(1 - x - y\) dz ] dy ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Innermost Integral \(with respect to z\):) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(1 - x - y\) dz = [ z ]_0^\(1 - x - y\) = 1 - x - y.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate the Middle Integral \(with respect to y\):) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(1 - x\) \(1 - x - y\) dy:) Tj
T*
(   Treat \(1 - x\) as a constant:) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(1 - x\)*y - y^2 / 2 ]_0^\(1 - x\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 - x\)*\(1 - x\) - \(1 - x\)^2 / 2) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 - x\)^2 - \(1/2\)*\(1 - x\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * \(1 - x\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Evaluate the Outermost Integral \(with respect to x\):) Tj
T*
(   V = int_0^1 \(1/2\) * \(1 - x\)^2 dx.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute u = 1 - x => du = -dx:) Tj
T*
(   V = \(1/2\) * [ - \(1 - x\)^3 / 3 ]_0^1) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * [ 0 - \(-1/3\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * \(1/3\) = 1/6.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The volume of the tetrahedron is 1/6.) Tj
T*
