(   [Problem Statement]: Explain cylindrical coordinates and evaluate the volume of the solid enclosed by the paraboloid z = x^2 + y^2 and the horizontal plane z = 4.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Cylindrical Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   - Transformation: x = r * cos theta, y = r * sin theta, z = z.) Tj
T*
(   - Volume element: dV = r dr dtheta dz.) Tj
T*
(   - Paraboloid equation: z = x^2 + y^2 = r^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Capping plane: z = 4.) Tj
T*
(   2. Limits of Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - For a fixed point \(r, theta\), z varies from the paraboloid surface z = r^2 up to the plane z) Tj
T*
(   = 4.) Tj
T*
(   - The intersection curve is r^2 = 4 => r = 2 \(a circle of radius 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Radial coordinate r ranges from 0 to 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Angular coordinate theta sweeps full circle from 0 to 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(   3. Formulation and Evaluation of Triple Integral:) Tj
T*
(   V = int_0^\(2*pi\) [ int_0^2 [ int_{r^2}^4 dz ] r dr ] dtheta.) Tj
T*
