(   [Problem Statement]: Explain spherical polar coordinates \(rho, theta, phi\) and evaluate the triple integral: I = iiint_V sqrt\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2\) dx dy dz over the sphere x^2 + y^2 + z^2 <= a^2.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Spherical Polar Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   - Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   x = rho * sin phi * cos theta) Tj
T*
(   y = rho * sin phi * sin theta) Tj
T*
(   z = rho * cos phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Radial distance: rho in [0, a].) Tj
T*
(   - Polar \(colatitude\) angle: phi in [0, pi] \(from north pole to south pole\).) Tj
T*
(   - Azimuthal angle: theta in [0, 2*pi] \(in xy-plane\).) Tj
T*
(   - Jacobian of transformation:) Tj
T*
(   J = rho^2 * sin phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Volume element: dV = rho^2 * sin phi drho dphi dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   2. Formulation of the Integral:) Tj
T*
(   - Integrand: sqrt\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2\) = rho.) Tj
T*
(   - I = int_0^\(2*pi\) dtheta * int_0^pi sin phi dphi * int_0^a rho * \(rho^2 * sin phi drho dphi) Tj
T*
(   dtheta\)) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^\(2*pi\) dtheta * int_0^pi sin phi dphi * int_0^a rho^3 drho.) Tj
T*
(   3. Factorized Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   - Factor 1 \(theta\): int_0^\(2*pi\) dtheta = 2 * pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Factor 2 \(phi\): int_0^pi sin phi dphi = [ -cos phi ]_0^pi = -cos\(pi\) - \(-cos 0\) = -\(-1\) + 1 =) Tj
T*
(   2.) Tj
T*
(   - Factor 3 \(rho\): int_0^a rho^3 drho = [ rho^4 / 4 ]_0^a = a^4 / 4.) Tj
T*
(   4. Multiply All Factors:) Tj
T*
(   I = \(2 * pi\) * \(2\) * \(a^4 / 4\)) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * pi * \(a^4 / 4\) = pi * a^4.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The value of the triple integral is pi * a^4.) Tj
T*
