(   [Problem Statement]: State Dirichlet's Theorem for triple integrals. Use it to evaluate: I = iiint_V x^\(l-1\) * y^\(m-1\) * z^\(n-1\) dx dy dz over the positive octant bounded by x + y + z <= 1 \(x, y, z >= 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Dirichlet's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let V be the closed tetrahedral region in the first octant bounded by the coordinate planes and) Tj
T*
(   the plane x + y + z = 1:) Tj
T*
(   V = { \(x, y, z\) : x >= 0, y >= 0, z >= 0, and x + y + z <= 1 }.) Tj
T*
(   Then for any l, m, n > 0:) Tj
T*
(   iiint_V x^\(l-1\) * y^\(m-1\) * z^\(n-1\) dx dy dz = [ Gamma\(l\) * Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(n\) ] / Gamma\(l + m) Tj
T*
(   + n + 1\).) Tj
T*
ET

