(   2. Derivation via Repeated Beta Integrals:) Tj
T*
(   - Limits: z from 0 to 1 - x - y; y from 0 to 1 - x; x from 0 to 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Inner integral with respect to z:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(1 - x - y\) z^\(n - 1\) dz = \(1 - x - y\)^n / n.) Tj
T*
(   - Middle integral with respect to y:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(1 - x\) y^\(m - 1\) * \(1 - x - y\)^n dy.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute y = \(1 - x\) * t => dy = \(1 - x\) dt:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^1 [ \(1 - x\)^\(m-1\) * t^\(m-1\) ] * [ \(1 - x\)^n * \(1 - t\)^n ] * \(1 - x\) dt) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 - x\)^\(m + n\) * int_0^1 t^\(m-1\) * \(1 - t\)^n dt) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 - x\)^\(m + n\) * Beta\(m, n + 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide by n: Beta\(m, n+1\)/n = [ Gamma\(m\)*Gamma\(n+1\) ] / [ n * Gamma\(m+n+1\) ]) Tj
T*
(   Since Gamma\(n+1\) = n*Gamma\(n\), this equals [ Gamma\(m\)*Gamma\(n\) ] / Gamma\(m+n+1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Outermost integral with respect to x:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^1 x^\(l - 1\) * \(1 - x\)^\(m + n\) dx = Beta\(l, m + n + 1\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ Gamma\(l\) * Gamma\(m + n + 1\) ] / Gamma\(l + m + n + 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Multiplying both factors cancels Gamma\(m + n + 1\):) Tj
T*
(   I = [ Gamma\(l\) * Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(n\) ] / Gamma\(l + m + n + 1\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
