(   [Problem Statement]: Find the volume common to the two intersecting cylinders of equal radius a: x^2 + y^2 = a^2 and x^2 + z^2 = a^2 \(Steinmetz solid\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Symmetry of the Solid:) Tj
T*
(   - The solid is bounded by y = +- sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) and z = +- sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - It is symmetric in all 8 octants.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Volume V = 8 * V_octant \(in the first octant where x, y, z >= 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Limits in the First Octant:) Tj
T*
(   - For any fixed \(x, y\), z ranges from 0 to sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the xy-plane, the projection is bounded by the circular quarter-disk:) Tj
T*
(   y ranges from 0 to sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   x ranges from 0 to a.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Set up Double Integral for Volume:) Tj
T*
(   V_octant = int_0^a [ int_0^sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) z dy ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^a [ int_0^sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) dy ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Evaluate Inner Integral with respect to y:) Tj
T*
(   Since sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) does not depend on y:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) dy = sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) * [ y ]_0^sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\)) Tj
T*
(   = sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\) * sqrt\(a^2 - x^2\)) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 - x^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Evaluate Outer Integral with respect to x:) Tj
T*
(   V_octant = int_0^a \(a^2 - x^2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ a^2 * x - x^3 / 3 ]_0^a) Tj
T*
(   = a^3 - a^3 / 3 = 2*a^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Compute Total Volume:) Tj
T*
(   V = 8 * V_octant = 8 * \(2*a^3 / 3\) = 16*a^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The volume common to the two cylinders is 16*a^3 / 3.) Tj
T*
