(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - The work done by a force field F along a directed curve C parametrized by r\(t\) for t in [t1,) Tj
T*
(   t2] is:) Tj
T*
(   W = int_C F . dr = int_{t1}^{t2} [ Fx * \(dx/dt\) + Fy * \(dy/dt\) + Fz * \(dz/dt\) ] dt.) Tj
T*
(   2. Parametric Expressions:) Tj
T*
(   - x = t => dx = dt.) Tj
T*
(   - y = t^2 => dy = 2t dt.) Tj
T*
(   - z = t^3 => dz = 3t^2 dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Limits: at \(0, 0, 0\), t = 0; at \(1, 1, 1\), t = 1.) Tj
T*
(   3. Express F in terms of parameter t:) Tj
T*
(   - Fx = 3x^2 + 6y = 3\(t^2\) + 6\(t^2\) = 9*t^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Fy = -14yz = -14\(t^2\)\(t^3\) = -14*t^5.) Tj
T*
(   - Fz = 20xz^2 = 20\(t\)\(t^3\)^2 = 20\(t\)\(t^6\) = 20*t^7.) Tj
T*
(   4. Form the Dot Product F . dr:) Tj
T*
(   F . dr = Fx*dx + Fy*dy + Fz*dz) Tj
T*
(   = \(9*t^2\)*dt + \(-14*t^5\)*\(2t dt\) + \(20*t^7\)*\(3t^2 dt\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(9*t^2 - 28*t^6 + 60*t^9\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   5. Integrate from t = 0 to t = 1:) Tj
T*
(   W = int_0^1 \(9*t^2 - 28*t^6 + 60*t^9\) dt) Tj
T*
(   = [ 9*\(t^3 / 3\) - 28*\(t^7 / 7\) + 60*\(t^10 / 10\) ]_0^1) Tj
T*
(   = [ 3*t^3 - 4*t^7 + 6*t^10 ]_0^1) Tj
T*
(   = [ 3\(1\) - 4\(1\) + 6\(1\) ] - 0) Tj
T*
(   = 3 - 4 + 6 = 5.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The total work done by the force field is 5 units.) Tj
T*
