/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define a conservative vector field. Prove that F = \(2xy + z^3\)*i + x^2*j + 3xz^2*k is conservative, find its scalar potential function phi\(x, y, z\), and evaluate the work done in moving from \(1, -2, 1\) to \(3, 1, 4\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Condition for Conservative Field:) Tj
T*
(   A vector field F is conservative if curl\(F\) = del x F = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute curl\(F\):) Tj
T*
(   | i j k |) Tj
T*
(   | d/dx d/dy d/dz |) Tj
T*
(   | 2xy+z^3 x^2 3xz^2 |) Tj
T*
(   i-component: d/dy\(3xz^2\) - d/dz\(x^2\) = 0 - 0 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   j-component: d/dz\(2xy+z^3\) - d/dx\(3xz^2\) = 3z^2 - 3z^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   k-component: d/dx\(x^2\) - d/dy\(2xy+z^3\) = 2x - 2x = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - curl\(F\) = 0. Thus F is strictly CONSERVATIVE.) Tj
T*
(   2. Find Scalar Potential phi such that F = grad\(phi\):) Tj
T*
(   - dphi/dx = 2xy + z^3 => phi = int \(2xy + z^3\) dx = x^2*y + x*z^3 + g\(y, z\).) Tj
T*
(   - dphi/dy = x^2 + dg/dy. Equating to Fy = x^2:) Tj
T*
(   x^2 + dg/dy = x^2 => dg/dy = 0 => g\(y, z\) = h\(z\).) Tj
T*
(   - dphi/dz = 3x*z^2 + dh/dz. Equating to Fz = 3x*z^2:) Tj
T*
(   3x*z^2 + dh/dz = 3x*z^2 => dh/dz = 0 => h\(z\) = C.) Tj
T*
(   - Potential Function:) Tj
T*
(   phi\(x, y, z\) = x^2 * y + x * z^3 + C.) Tj
T*
(   3. Work Done from A\(1, -2, 1\) to B\(3, 1, 4\):) Tj
T*
(   By the Fundamental Theorem for Line Integrals:) Tj
T*
(   W = int_A^B F . dr = phi\(B\) - phi\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   - phi\(B\) = phi\(3, 1, 4\) = \(3^2\)\(1\) + \(3\)\(4^3\) = 9 + 3\(64\) = 9 + 192 = 201.) Tj
T*
(   - phi\(A\) = phi\(1, -2, 1\) = \(1^2\)\(-2\) + \(1\)\(1^3\) = -2 + 1 = -1.) Tj
T*
ET

