(>> Solution to Question 17:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State Green's Theorem in a plane. Provide a complete analytical proof for a simple region R bounded by a piecewise smooth curve C.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Statement of Green's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let C be a positively oriented \(counter-clockwise\), piecewise smooth, simple closed curve in) Tj
T*
(   the xy-plane bounding a region R.) Tj
T*
(   If P\(x, y\) and Q\(x, y\) have continuous partial derivatives in an open region containing R,) Tj
T*
(   then:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C \(P dx + Q dy\) = iint_R [ dQ/dx - dP/dy ] dA.) Tj
T*
(   2. Complete Analytical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   It suffices to prove the two component equations separately:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. A\) oint_C P dx = - iint_R \(dP/dy\) dA.) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. B\) oint_C Q dy = iint_R \(dQ/dx\) dA.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof of Eq. A \(Type I region\):) Tj
T*
(   Let R be bounded below by y = g1\(x\) and above by y = g2\(x\) for x in [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   The boundary C consists of four smooth curves: C1 \(bottom, x from a to b\), C2 \(right vertical) Tj
T*
(   line\), C3 \(top, x from b to a\), and C4 \(left vertical line\).) Tj
T*
(   Evaluate the double integral on the right of Eq. A:) Tj
T*
(   iint_R \(dP/dy\) dA = int_a^b [ int_{g1\(x\)}^{g2\(x\)} \(dP/dy\) dy ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_a^b [ P\(x, g2\(x\)\) - P\(x, g1\(x\)\) ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Now evaluate the line integral oint_C P dx:) Tj
T*
(   * Along C1 \(y = g1\(x\)\): int_{C1} P dx = int_a^b P\(x, g1\(x\)\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   * Along C2 and C4 \(vertical lines x = b and x = a\): dx = 0, so integrals are 0.) Tj
T*
(   * Along C3 \(y = g2\(x\), traversed right-to-left from b to a\):) Tj
T*
(   int_{C3} P dx = int_b^a P\(x, g2\(x\)\) dx = - int_a^b P\(x, g2\(x\)\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   Summing along all curves:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C P dx = int_a^b P\(x, g1\(x\)\) dx - int_a^b P\(x, g2\(x\)\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = - int_a^b [ P\(x, g2\(x\)\) - P\(x, g1\(x\)\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = - iint_R \(dP/dy\) dA. \(Eq. A proved\).) Tj
T*
(   - Proof of Eq. B \(Type II region\):) Tj
T*
(   By treating R as a region bounded by x = h1\(y\) and x = h2\(y\) for y in [c, d] and repeating the) Tj
T*
(   exact argument:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C Q dy = iint_R \(dQ/dx\) dA. \(Eq. B proved\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adding Eq. A and Eq. B:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C \(P dx + Q dy\) = iint_R [ dQ/dx - dP/dy ] dA.) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
