(   - dQ/dx = d/dx [ x^2 ] = 2x.) Tj
T*
(   - dP/dy = d/dy [ xy + y^2 ] = x + 2y.) Tj
T*
(   - dQ/dx - dP/dy = 2x - \(x + 2y\) = x - 2y.) Tj
T*
(   - In region R: for a given x in [0, 1], y ranges from the parabola y = x^2 \(lower\) to line y =) Tj
T*
(   x \(upper\).) Tj
T*
(   - iint_R \(x - 2y\) dA = int_0^1 [ int_{x^2}^x \(x - 2y\) dy ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Inner integral:) Tj
T*
(   int_{x^2}^x \(x - 2y\) dy = [ x*y - y^2 ]_{x^2}^x) Tj
T*
(   = [ x\(x\) - x^2 ] - [ x\(x^2\) - \(x^2\)^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ x^2 - x^2 ] - [ x^3 - x^4 ] = -x^3 + x^4.) Tj
T*
(   - Outer integral:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^1 \(-x^3 + x^4\) dx = [ -x^4 / 4 + x^5 / 5 ]_0^1 = -1/4 + 1/5 = -5/20 + 4/20 = -1/20.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Line Integral oint_C \(P dx + Q dy\):) Tj
T*
(   Boundary C consists of C1 \(parabola y = x^2 from 0 to 1\) and C2 \(line y = x from 1 to 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Along C1: y = x^2 => dy = 2x dx.) Tj
T*
(   int_{C1} = int_0^1 [ \(x\(x^2\) + \(x^2\)^2\) dx + x^2 * \(2x dx\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^1 [ \(x^3 + x^4\) + 2x^3 ] dx = int_0^1 \(3x^3 + x^4\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ 3*x^4 / 4 + x^5 / 5 ]_0^1 = 3/4 + 1/5 = 15/20 + 4/20 = 19/20.) Tj
T*
(   - Along C2: y = x => dy = dx \(x traverses from 1 to 0\):) Tj
T*
(   int_{C2} = int_1^0 [ \(x\(x\) + x^2\) dx + x^2 dx ] = int_1^0 [ 2x^2 + x^2 ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_1^0 3x^2 dx = [ x^3 ]_1^0 = 0 - 1 = -1 = -20/20.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Line Integral:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C = int_{C1} + int_{C2} = 19/20 - 20/20 = -1/20.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Line Integral \(-1/20\) = Double Integral \(-1/20\). Green's Theorem is fully verified.) Tj
