(>> Solution to Question 19:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the line integral area formula from Green's Theorem: Area = \(1/2\) * oint_C \(x dy - y dx\). Apply this formula to find the area enclosed by the astroid: x = a*cos^3\(t\), y = a*sin^3\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Area Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Green's Theorem: oint_C \(P dx + Q dy\) = iint_R \(dQ/dx - dP/dy\) dA.) Tj
T*
(   - Choose P = -y and Q = x:) Tj
T*
(   dP/dy = -1, dQ/dx = 1.) Tj
T*
(   dQ/dx - dP/dy = 1 - \(-1\) = 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute into Green's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C \(-y dx + x dy\) = iint_R 2 dA = 2 * iint_R 1 dA = 2 * Area\(R\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide by 2:) Tj
T*
(   Area\(R\) = \(1/2\) * oint_C \(x dy - y dx\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Application to Astroid: x = a*cos^3 t, y = a*sin^3 t \(t in [0, 2*pi]\):) Tj
T*
(   - Compute differentials:) Tj
T*
(   dx = -3a * cos^2 t * sin t dt.) Tj
T*
(   dy = 3a * sin^2 t * cos t dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Form x dy - y dx:) Tj
T*
(   x dy = \(a * cos^3 t\) * \(3a * sin^2 t * cos t dt\) = 3*a^2 * cos^4 t * sin^2 t dt.) Tj
T*
(   -y dx = - \(a * sin^3 t\) * \(-3a * cos^2 t * sin t dt\) = 3*a^2 * sin^4 t * cos^2 t dt.) Tj
T*
(   x dy - y dx = 3*a^2 * sin^2 t * cos^2 t * \(cos^2 t + sin^2 t\) dt) Tj
T*
(   = 3*a^2 * sin^2 t * cos^2 t dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate from t = 0 to 2*pi:) Tj
T*
(   Area = \(1/2\) * int_0^\(2*pi\) 3*a^2 * sin^2 t * cos^2 t dt) Tj
T*
(   = \(3*a^2 / 2\) * 4 * int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^2 t * cos^2 t dt \(by symmetry in 4 quadrants\)) Tj
T*
(   = 6*a^2 * [ \(1\)\(1\) / \(4\)\(2\) ] * \(pi / 2\) \(using Wallis' formula\)) Tj
T*
(   = 6*a^2 * [ 1 / 8 ] * \(pi / 2\)) Tj
T*
ET

