(   - On S1: \(curl F\) . n = k . k = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - iint_{S1} \(curl F\) . n dS = iint_{S1} 1 dA = Area of unit disk = pi * \(1\)^2 = pi.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Line Integral oint_C F . dr:) Tj
T*
(   - Boundary C is the circle x^2 + y^2 = 1, z = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Parametric equations: x = cos t, y = sin t, z = 0 \(t in [0, 2*pi]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Differentials: dx = -sin t dt, dy = cos t dt, dz = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - F on C \(with z = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Fx = 2x - y = 2*cos t - sin t.) Tj
T*
(   Fy = -y*z^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Fz = -y^2*z = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - F . dr = Fx * dx = \(2*cos t - sin t\) * \(-sin t dt\)) Tj
T*
(   = \( -2*sin t * cos t + sin^2 t \) dt) Tj
T*
(   = [ -sin\(2t\) + \(1 - cos 2t\)/2 ] dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate from 0 to 2*pi:) Tj
T*
(   oint_C F . dr = int_0^\(2*pi\) [ -sin\(2t\) + 1/2 - \(1/2\)*cos\(2t\) ] dt) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(1/2\)*cos\(2t\) + t/2 - \(1/4\)*sin\(2t\) ]_0^\(2*pi\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(1/2\) + pi - 0 ] - [ 1/2 + 0 - 0 ] = pi.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Surface Integral \(pi\) = Line Integral \(pi\). Stokes' Theorem is completely verified.) Tj
