(>> Solution to Question 22:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State Gauss' Divergence Theorem. Provide a rigorous analytical proof for a simple 3D volume V bounded by an orientable closed surface S.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Statement of Gauss' Divergence Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let V be a compact, solid volume in R^3 bounded by a piecewise smooth, closed orientable) Tj
T*
(   surface S.) Tj
T*
(   Let n be the outward unit normal vector field on S.) Tj
T*
(   If F = F1*i + F2*j + F3*k is a vector field with continuous first partial derivatives in an) Tj
T*
(   open region containing V, then:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S F . n dS = iiint_V div\(F\) dV = iiint_V [ dF1/dx + dF2/dy + dF3/dz ] dV.) Tj
T*
(   2. Analytical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   It suffices to establish the three component equations separately:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 1\) iint_S F3 * \(n . k\) dS = iiint_V \(dF3/dz\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 2\) iint_S F2 * \(n . j\) dS = iiint_V \(dF2/dy\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 3\) iint_S F1 * \(n . i\) dS = iiint_V \(dF1/dx\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof of Eq. 1:) Tj
T*
(   Let V be a z-simple region bounded below by surface z = z1\(x, y\) \(surface S1\) and above by z =) Tj
T*
(   z2\(x, y\) \(surface S2\) over a plane region R in the xy-plane, plus a vertical cylinder S3.) Tj
T*
(   Evaluate the triple integral on the right:) Tj
T*
(   iiint_V \(dF3/dz\) dV = iint_R [ int_{z1\(x, y\)}^{z2\(x, y\)} \(dF3/dz\) dz ] dA) Tj
T*
(   = iint_R [ F3\(x, y, z2\(x, y\)\) - F3\(x, y, z1\(x, y\)\) ] dA.) Tj
T*
(   Now evaluate the surface flux integral of F3*k over the closed boundary S = S1 + S2 + S3:) Tj
T*
(   * On upper surface S2: the upward normal has n . k > 0, and \(n . k\) dS = dA:) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S2} F3*\(n . k\) dS = iint_R F3\(x, y, z2\(x, y\)\) dA.) Tj
T*
(   * On lower surface S1: the downward normal has n . k < 0, and \(n . k\) dS = -dA:) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S1} F3*\(n . k\) dS = - iint_R F3\(x, y, z1\(x, y\)\) dA.) Tj
T*
(   * On lateral cylindrical surface S3: the normal n is horizontal, so n . k = 0:) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S3} F3*\(n . k\) dS = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Summing over S:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S F3*\(n . k\) dS = iint_R [ F3\(x, y, z2\) - F3\(x, y, z1\) ] dA = iiint_V \(dF3/dz\) dV. \(Eq. 1) Tj
T*
(   proved\).) Tj
T*
(   - Proving Eq. 2 and Eq. 3 similarly by projecting onto the xz and yz planes and adding all) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
