(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Verify Gauss' Divergence Theorem for the vector field F = 4x*i - 2y^2*j + z^2*k over the cylinder x^2 + y^2 = 4, bounded by z = 0 and z = 3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute div\(F\):) Tj
T*
(   F = 4x*i - 2y^2*j + z^2*k.) Tj
T*
(   div\(F\) = d/dx\(4x\) + d/dy\(-2y^2\) + d/dz\(z^2\) = 4 - 4y + 2z.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Evaluate the Volume Integral iiint_V div\(F\) dV:) Tj
T*
(   - Use cylindrical coordinates: x = r*cos theta, y = r*sin theta, z = z.) Tj
T*
(   dV = r dr dtheta dz.) Tj
T*
(   r ranges from 0 to 2; theta ranges from 0 to 2*pi; z ranges from 0 to 3.) Tj
T*
(   - div\(F\) = 4 - 4*r*sin theta + 2z.) Tj
T*
(   - iiint_V \(4 - 4*r*sin theta + 2z\) r dr dtheta dz:) Tj
T*
(   Split into three terms:) Tj
T*
(   * Term 1: int_0^\(2*pi\) dtheta * int_0^2 4r dr * int_0^3 dz) Tj
T*
(   = \(2*pi\) * [ 2*r^2 ]_0^2 * [ z ]_0^3 = \(2*pi\) * 8 * 3 = 48*pi.) Tj
T*
(   * Term 2: int_0^\(2*pi\) sin theta dtheta * int_0^2 \(-4r^2\) dr * int_0^3 dz) Tj
T*
(   Since int_0^\(2*pi\) sin theta dtheta = 0, Term 2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   * Term 3: int_0^\(2*pi\) dtheta * int_0^2 r dr * int_0^3 2z dz) Tj
T*
(   = \(2*pi\) * [ r^2 / 2 ]_0^2 * [ z^2 ]_0^3 = \(2*pi\) * 2 * 9 = 36*pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Volume Integral:) Tj
T*
(   iiint_V div\(F\) dV = 48*pi + 0 + 36*pi = 84*pi.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate Surface Integral over Closed Cylinder S = S1 + S2 + S3:) Tj
T*
(   - S1 \(Top disc z = 3, n = k\):) Tj
T*
(   F . n = Fz = z^2 = 3^2 = 9.) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S1} 9 dS = 9 * Area\(S1\) = 9 * \(pi * 2^2\) = 36*pi.) Tj
T*
(   - S2 \(Bottom disc z = 0, n = -k\):) Tj
T*
(   F . n = -Fz = -z^2 = -0 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S2} 0 dS = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - S3 \(Curved side x^2 + y^2 = 4, r = 2, n = \(x*i + y*j\)/2\):) Tj
T*
(   F . n = [ 4x*\(x/2\) - 2y^2*\(y/2\) ] = 2*x^2 - y^3 = 2*\(2*cos theta\)^2 - \(2*sin theta\)^3) Tj
T*
(   = 8*cos^2 theta - 8*sin^3 theta.) Tj
T*
(   dS = 2 dtheta dz.) Tj
T*
(   iint_{S3} F . n dS = int_0^3 dz * int_0^\(2*pi\) [ 8*cos^2 theta - 8*sin^3 theta ] * 2 dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = 3 * 2 * [ 8 * int_0^\(2*pi\) cos^2 theta dtheta - 8 * 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 6 * [ 8 * pi ] = 48*pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Surface Integral:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S F . n dS = 36*pi + 0 + 48*pi = 84*pi.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Volume Integral \(84*pi\) = Surface Integral \(84*pi\). Gauss' Divergence Theorem is verified.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
