(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the surface integral iint_S F . n dS, where F = z*i + x*j - 3y^2*z*k and S is the surface of the cylinder x^2 + y^2 = 16 included in the first octant between z = 0 and z = 5.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Parametrize the Cylindrical Surface S:) Tj
T*
(   - Since x^2 + y^2 = 16, radius R = 4.) Tj
T*
(   - In the first octant: x >= 0, y >= 0 => theta in [0, pi/2].) Tj
T*
(   - Parametric equations:) Tj
T*
(   x = 4 * cos theta, y = 4 * sin theta, z = z \(where 0 <= z <= 5\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute Normal Vector n and Surface Element dS:) Tj
T*
(   - Outward unit normal: n = \(x*i + y*j\) / 4 = cos theta * i + sin theta * j + 0 * k.) Tj
T*
(   - Area element: dS = 4 dtheta dz.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate Dot Product F . n:) Tj
T*
(   - F = z * i + x * j - 3y^2*z * k) Tj
T*
(   = z * i + \(4 * cos theta\) * j - 3*\(16 * sin^2 theta\)*z * k.) Tj
T*
(   - F . n = \(z * cos theta\) + \(4 * cos theta * sin theta\) + 0) Tj
T*
(   = z * cos theta + 4 * sin theta * cos theta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Set up the Double Integral:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S F . n dS = int_0^5 [ int_0^\(pi/2\) \(z * cos theta + 4 * sin theta * cos theta\) * 4 dtheta) Tj
T*
(   ] dz) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * int_0^5 [ int_0^\(pi/2\) \(z * cos theta + 2 * sin 2theta\) dtheta ] dz.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Evaluate Inner Integral with respect to theta:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(pi/2\) \(z * cos theta + 2 * sin 2theta\) dtheta = [ z * sin theta - cos 2theta ]_0^\(pi/2\)) Tj
T*
(   - At pi/2: z*sin\(pi/2\) - cos\(pi\) = z\(1\) - \(-1\) = z + 1.) Tj
T*
(   - At 0: z*sin\(0\) - cos\(0\) = 0 - 1 = -1.) Tj
T*
(   - Difference: \(z + 1\) - \(-1\) = z + 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Evaluate Outer Integral with respect to z:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S F . n dS = 4 * int_0^5 \(z + 2\) dz) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * [ z^2 / 2 + 2z ]_0^5) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * [ 25/2 + 10 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * [ 45 / 2 ] = 2 * 45 = 90.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
