(   iiint_V \(drho / dt\) dV = - iint_S \(rho * v\) . n dS.) Tj
T*
(   3. Application of Gauss' Divergence Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - Transform the surface integral into a volume integral:) Tj
T*
(   iint_S \(rho * v\) . n dS = iiint_V div\(rho * v\) dV.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   iiint_V \(drho / dt\) dV = - iiint_V div\(rho * v\) dV) Tj
T*
(   => iiint_V [ drho / dt + div\(rho * v\) ] dV = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since volume V is completely arbitrary, the integrand must vanish identically everywhere:) Tj
T*
(   drho / dt + div\(rho * v\) = 0 \(The Continuity Equation\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Incompressible Fluid Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - For an incompressible liquid broth, fluid density rho is strictly constant \(drho/dt = 0 and) Tj
T*
(   grad\(rho\) = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   div\(rho * v\) = rho * div\(v\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since rho != 0:) Tj
T*
(   div\(v\) = 0. \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The velocity field of an incompressible fluid is strictly solenoidal.) Tj
