(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In biotechnology bioreactor design, use surface flux integration to calculate the total oxygen mass transfer rate across spherical gas bubbles of uniform radius R = 1 mm. Given gas holdup epsilon_g = 0.1, liquid volume V_L = 10 m^3, mass transfer coefficient k_L = 4 * 10^-4 m/s, and concentration driving force Delta_C = 0.2 mol/m^3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Model of Bubble Interfacial Flux:) Tj
T*
(   - The oxygen flux through the gas-liquid interface S_b of a single spherical bubble is:) Tj
T*
(   J_O2 = k_L * Delta_C.) Tj
T*
(   - Total oxygen mass transfer rate across one bubble:) Tj
T*
(   Q_single = iint_{S_b} J_O2 dS = k_L * Delta_C * iint_{S_b} 1 dS) Tj
T*
(   = k_L * Delta_C * \(4 * pi * R^2\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Number of Bubbles in the Bioreactor:) Tj
T*
(   - Volume of one bubble:) Tj
T*
(   V_b = \(4/3\) * pi * R^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Total gas volume in bioreactor:) Tj
T*
(   V_gas = epsilon_g * V_L = 0.1 * 10 m^3 = 1.0 m^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Total count of bubbles:) Tj
T*
(   N_b = V_gas / V_b = V_gas / [ \(4/3\) * pi * R^3 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Total Interfacial Surface Area \(a_total\):) Tj
T*
(   - A_total = N_b * \(4 * pi * R^2\) = [ V_gas / \(\(4/3\)*pi*R^3\) ] * \(4*pi*R^2\)) Tj
T*
(   = 3 * V_gas / R.) Tj
T*
(   - With R = 1 mm = 10^-3 m:) Tj
T*
(   A_total = 3 * \(1.0 m^3\) / 10^-3 m = 3000 m^2.) Tj
T*
(   4. Total Oxygen Transfer Rate \(OTR\):) Tj
T*
(   - OTR = iint_{A_total} J_O2 dS = k_L * Delta_C * A_total.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute numerical values:) Tj
T*
(   OTR = \(4 * 10^-4 m/s\) * \(0.2 mol/m^3\) * \(3000 m^2\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(4 * 10^-4\) * 0.2 * 3000) Tj
T*
(   = 0.08 * 3 = 0.24 mol/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Converting to mol/hour:) Tj
T*
(   OTR = 0.24 * 3600 = 864 mol/h.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The total oxygen transfer rate integrated across all bubbles is 0.24 mol/s \(864 mol/h\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
